    "title": "Oroville's 1911 Ehmann Home Needs $100K Fix Before It Crumbles Further - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elisa Nguyen ,\n1 days ago The Ehmann Home in Oroville has stood since 1911, a Craftsman bungalow tied to the woman remembered as the mother of California's ripe-olive industry, and now it needs extensive repairs just to stay standing. The Butte County Historical Society, which owns and maintains the property, is hoping a dinner fundraiser this Saturday can help cover the cost before deterioration goes any further. Read full article\n3",
